# Session document rebuild (Oct 2026)

Structural entity changes rebuild the Remote Compose document; variable updates do not.

## Anti-flash

- `ScreenRenderer.render(..., initialPage = …)` — bake the tablet’s current page into `Vars.PAGE` so a rebuild does not open on home before the player restores page.
- Player: hide / keep prior frame while the new document swaps (`RemoteDocumentView`).
- Prefer vars for live values. Timed `refreshEvery` on media (etc.) caused home flashes — only use when the document tree itself must change (forecast lists, to-do rows).

## Helpers

- `RenderedDoc.structureChanged` / `isTimedRefreshDue` — split from `stale` for clearer session host logic.
- Thermostat: mode in `structural` when layout depends on `usesDualSetpoint()` so Heat ↔ Heat/Cool rebuilds the dial keys.

## Scroll survives a rebuild

One document holds every page. Replacing it used to start every `verticalScroll` / `horizontalScroll` at the top, so a thermostat state change or a calendar timer jumped the lights lists (and every other list) even though the chosen room stayed.

- `keptVerticalScroll` / `keptHorizontalScroll` (`ScrollKeep.kt`) put a stable component id on each scroller. Ids are `0x60_0000` plus a hash of a name (`lights.<tile>.rooms`, `calendar.<tile>`, `freeform.<node>`, …), above video (`0x5C`), map (`0x5D`) and search (`0x5E`).
- The player copies those offsets onto the new document (`DocumentScroll.kt`) before the swap is shown. The position float is what paint reads; the touch expression would otherwise write 0 back until the next drag.
- When the new bytes match the document already on screen, `SessionDocument.show` keeps that document and only sends changed vars and pictures. The revision stays, so taps still match.
